--TEST--
A value an `Ldap\Entry` returns is `tainted`, so `string`'s result does not compile as a search `base` — ADR 0278 § 5 and § 6 and `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Reports {
    public static function under(Core\Ldap\Connection $corp, Core\Ldap\Entry $manager): void {
        var $base = $manager->string("distinguishedName");
        if ($base != null) {
            var $found = $corp->search(Core\Ldap\Filter::present("cn"), {base: $base});
        }
    }
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string|Core\Ldap\Dn`, found `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:6:80
%A
  = help: a `tainted` DN is a sink: build it with `Core\Ldap\Dn::of($attribute, $value)` or `$dn->child($attribute, $value)`, which escape the value and return the `Core\Ldap\Dn` this parameter accepts

